compat: Runner B (ARM64 Wine + FEX) as its own Steam tool, and a run script that serves both runners.

steamplay-mac. Before this, the dylib declared one tool, "notproton", whose run script always
used runners/current and found the loader only as wine.app or x86_64-unix/wine, so Runner B
(Highball loader layout) could not be launched from Steam.

- compat.c: a second tool, "notproton-fex" ("Steam Play (Wine, FEX)"), written next to
  "notproton" (now shown as "Steam Play (Wine, Rosetta)") with the same run script. It is
  declared only while runners/current-fex/runner.json exists, and withdrawn otherwise. The name
  keeps "proton" so Steam Cloud's path mapping still applies.
- compat_run.sh:
  - the tool directory (resolved: Steam runs '<dir>/.'/run) picks the runner (notproton -> runners/current, notproton-fex ->
    runners/current-fex);
  - runner.json "loader"/"server"/"unix_dir" (relative, inside the runner) name the loader,
    wineserver and unix dir when present; WINEDLLPATH uses aarch64-windows for them;
  - an arm64 runner never gets D3DMetal (none exists for arm64) and gets DXMT only when
    lib/renderers/dxmt/aarch64-unix/winemetal.so is present; otherwise wined3d, logged;
  - Game Mode staging symlinks a loader that is itself a link (Highball's entitled loader keeps
    its provisioning profile only when run in place; a hard link or copy loses it);
  - an arm64 runner keeps its own lsteamclient (the bridge copy is the Rosetta runner's);
  - switching a game between tools parks the other runner's prefix as pfx.<machine> and
    restores this runner's, instead of refusing; it waits up to 15 s for the old wineserver;
  - an arm64 runner gets no Steam overlay injection for now (its dylibs break Wine's
    shared user data mapping, c0000018, and the game exits at once);
  - an arm64 runner sets FEX_HOSTFEATURES (enablecrc/enablecrypto from sysctl FEAT_CRC32,
    FEAT_AES+FEAT_PMULL; Wine on macOS publishes no ID registers, so FEX hid SSE4.2/AES-NI/PCLMUL),
    forwarded to the game;
  - on an arm64 runner the registry batch marks Steam's Jun2010 DirectX redist as run (its
    DXSETUP never exits on a new FEX prefix and holds the evaluator); NOTPROTON_FEX_DXSETUP=1 opts
    back in (Phase 4 phase4-fex-skip-dxsetup);
  - on an arm64 runner an Unreal Engine bootstrap (<Name>.exe next to Engine/) is replaced by
    <Name>/Binaries/Win64/<Name>-Win64-Shipping.exe (the bootstrap always finds the VC runtime
    missing there and exits after its prerequisites setup);
  - on the Vulkan route the pipeline caches go under Steam's shadercache/<appid>
    (STEAM_COMPAT_SHADER_PATH): vkd3d-proton's pipeline library (VKD3D_SHADER_CACHE_PATH, a
    Windows path) and Mesa's disk cache for KosmicKrisp (MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR). Left to itself
    vkd3d-proton used the game's directory and wrote nothing, so every start recompiled every
    pipeline (Librarian: about three minutes behind a black window);
  - the syshud label says FEX or Rosetta from runner.json "flavour";
  - the per-launch registry values go in with one reg import (Phase 4 batch-prefix-registry);
  - Direct3D 12 on an arm64 runner: vkd3d-proton with DXVK's dxgi on KosmicKrisp, picked when
    lib/renderers/{vkd3d-proton,dxvk}/aarch64-windows (PE files marked builtin) and
    lib/renderers/kosmickrisp/{icd.d/kosmickrisp_icd.json,vklib/libMoltenVK.dylib} are present;
    the DXVK choice uses KosmicKrisp too. VK_DRIVER_FILES is set and forwarded, and the launcher
    sets DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH to vklib (winevulkan opens libMoltenVK.dylib, here the Vulkan loader).

